## GUIDEBOOK BIOME DESCRIPTION
guidebook.auroral_garden.body=The Auroral Garden is a winter wonderland filled with icy iris flowers that light up the night with colors resembling an aurora. Pale oak shrubs and natural prismarine deposits can also be found here.
guidebook.bayou.body=The Bayou is a subtropical swamp biome with waterlogged willow trees that have lush Spanish moss hanging down from them.
guidebook.bog.body=The Bog is a colder swamp biome with loads of sweet berry bushes and mangrove shrubs growing between the boggy ponds.
guidebook.cold_desert.body=The Cold Desert is a frozen waste consisting primarily of gravel, with patches of dead grass and hazardous powder snow. Polar bears are the only wildlife that can be found here.
guidebook.coniferous_forest.body=The Coniferous Forest is a serene, temperate forest biome with tall fir trees. Various flowers and foliage can be found on the ground below.
guidebook.crag.body=Crags are jagged mountains made up of several different kinds of stone, blanketed by patches of moss. Emerald ore can also be found here.
guidebook.dead_forest.body=The Dead Forest is a cold, dreary forest with dead trees and decaying brown foliage.
guidebook.dryland.body=The Dryland is a hot, dry brushland that's said to have strong prehistoric ties. Scattered pine trees and tiny cacti can be found growing here.
guidebook.dune_beach.body=Dune Beaches are the perfect place to enjoy beautiful ocean views amongst wavy sea oats and dune grass.
guidebook.field.body=The Field is an alpine meadow with spruce trees and shrubs, patches of white lavender, and plenty of other flowers!
guidebook.fir_clearing.body=The Fir Clearing is a variant of the Coniferous Forest that has shorter trees and fallen fir logs.
guidebook.forested_field.body=The Forested Field is a variant of the Field with an abundance of spruce trees and sprouts.
guidebook.fungal_jungle.body=The Fungal Jungle is a funky fest of fungi fun! Huge toadstools, patches of mycelium, dripstone spires, and more can be found in this bizarre biome.
guidebook.glowing_grotto.body=The Glowing Grotto is a cave biome illuminated by glowshrooms, glowing moss, and glowworm silk that hangs from the cavern ceilings!
guidebook.gravel_beach.body=Gravel Beaches are low-lying beaches made up of gravel, and nothing but gravel!
guidebook.highland.body=The Highland is a grassy biome that generates at higher elevations, with scattered boulders of mossy cobblestone. Emerald ore can also be found here.
guidebook.jade_cliffs.body=The Jade Cliffs are forested ridges with pine trees and spruce shrubs under a drab, jade sky. Emerald ore can also be found here.
guidebook.lavender_field.body=Lavender Fields are ripe with lush purple lavender and the occasional jacaranda tree.
guidebook.lush_desert.body=The Lush Desert is made up of orange sand, with ample amounts of dune grass, sparse acacia trees, and even the occasional palm tree! It can even rain here, unlike most deserts.
guidebook.lush_savanna.body=The Lush Savanna is a less sandy variant of the Lush Desert, with loads of poppies and flower buds.
guidebook.maple_woods.body=The Maple Woods are cold forests of red maple and spruce trees, with scattered violets and leaf litter that decorate the ground.
guidebook.mediterranean_forest.body=The Mediterranean Forest is a warm, coastal biome with cypress and dark oak trees, and a variety of other plants. Calcite can be found bordering the shores here.
guidebook.moor.body=The Moor is a wetter variant of the Highland, with scattered foliage and flowers. Emerald ore can also be found here.
guidebook.muskeg.body=The Muskeg is a snowy yet swampy biome with dead trees, patches of mud and podzol, and large brown mushrooms.
guidebook.mystic_grove.body=The Mystic Grove is a magical forest with cyan grass, glowflowers, blue magic trees, and more!
guidebook.old_growth_dead_forest.body=The Old Growth Dead Forest is a variant of the Dead Forest with taller trees and patches of podzol.
guidebook.old_growth_woodland.body=The Old Growth Woodland is a variant of the Woodland with bigger oak trees and patches of coarse dirt.
guidebook.ominous_woods.body=The Ominous Woods are dark, spooky forests with tall umbran trees that loom overhead. Illagers are rumored to be very fond of these woods...
guidebook.orchard.body=The Orchard is a fertile mix between a forest and grassland with flowering oak and azalea trees.
guidebook.origin_valley.body=The Origin Valley is a remnant of a time long past...These elusive islands are said to evoke a strong feeling of nostalgia in those who come across them.
guidebook.overgrown_greens.body=The Overgrown Greens are lush thickets teeming with huge flowers, clover petals, and high grass!
guidebook.pasture.body=The Pasture is a variant of the Prairie, made up of golden fields of barley as far as the eye can see!
guidebook.prairie.body=The Prairie is a relatively dry grassland with goldenrod flowers, sparse oak trees, and rooty stumps.
guidebook.pumpkin_patch.body=The Pumpkin Patch is a variant of the Seasonal Forest with pumpkins both big and small, barley, and other autumnal foliage.
guidebook.rainforest.body=The Rainforest is a humid, tropical jungle with mahogany trees, small jungle trees, pitcher plants, and other exotic foliage!
guidebook.redwood_forest.body=Redwood Forests have massive redwood trees towering over the podzol, moss, and ferns that cover the forest floor.
guidebook.rocky_rainforest.body=The Rocky Rainforest is a hilly variant of the Rainforest that has jacaranda trees and colorful gradients of terracotta.
guidebook.rocky_shrubland.body=The Rocky Shrubland is a hilly variant of the Shrubland that has exposed stone basins.
guidebook.scrubland.body=The Scrubland is a hot, flat grassland with patchy scrubs, purple wildflowers, and mounds of packed mud.
guidebook.seasonal_forest.body=Seasonal Forests are the perfect representation of autumn, with red, orange, and yellow maple trees, leaf litter, and marigold flowers!
guidebook.shrubland.body=The Shrubland is a mellow biome that tends to generate in flatter, low-lying areas, with lots of oak shrubs, bushes, and lilacs.
guidebook.snowblossom_grove.body=The Snowblossom Grove is an unusually lush forest of snow-covered snowblossom trees, with white petal flowers and mossy boulders covering the ground below.
guidebook.snowy_coniferous_forest.body=The Snowy Coniferous Forest is a snowy variant of the Coniferous Forest with violet flowers, and less trees overall.
guidebook.snowy_fir_clearing.body=The Snowy Fir Clearing is a snowy variant of the Fir Clearing with violet flowers, and less trees overall.
guidebook.snowy_maple_woods.body=The Snowy Maple Woods is a snowy variant of the Maple Woods that has less trees overall.
guidebook.spider_nest.body=The Spider Nest is a cave biome that spiders love to call home, cluttered with cobwebs of every kind, and spider eggs that may hatch if you're not careful!
guidebook.subtropics.body=The Subtropics are a transitional zone between temperate and tropical climates, with a variety of trees and plants, and large clay deposits.
guidebook.tropics.body=The Tropics are an island paradise littered with palm trees, pink hibiscus, bamboo, and plenty of other plants! White sand beaches line the coasts, leading out into crystal blue waters.
guidebook.tundra.body=The Tundra is a frigid, desolate plain dotted in woody tundra shrubs and mossy rocks. Not much wildlife can be found here aside from the occasional wolf.
guidebook.volcanic_plains.body=Volcanic Plains can often be found near Volcanoes, and consist of black sand that has a variety of foliage growing on it. Cooled pools of obsidian can also be found on the surface.
guidebook.volcano.body=Volcanoes are dangerous, molten mountains with lava lakes, magma, basalt, and volcanic ash. Emerald ore can also be found here.
guidebook.wasteland_steppe.body=The Wasteland Steppe is a grassier variant of the Wasteland that generates at higher altitudes, and is less barren overall.
guidebook.wasteland.body=The Wasteland is a barren desert consisting of dried salt and dead trees, with the occasional wilted lily sprouting up from the cracked ground.
guidebook.wetland.body=The Wetland is a swampy forest consisting of willow and spruce trees, with mud-lined banks, cattails, and other foliage.
guidebook.wintry_origin_valley.body=The Wintry Origin Valley is a snowy variant of the Origin Valley. Some question its existence due to how rare it is...
guidebook.woodland.body=The Woodland is a warm forest made up exclusively of oak trees and fallen logs.

